  "body": "https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/044900af6cc441d700d171098812786b4b312f59/synapse/handlers/e2e_room_keys.py#L300-L310\r\n\r\nSpecifically, given the above flow, if the new key has a worse (larger) `first_message_index`, and can thus decrypt a smaller number of messages, we will still overwrite the old key if the new key has a lesser `forwarded_count`. This could in some (probably rare) situations lead to data loss.",
